I’d keep it simple by using a one-page AI Risk Assessment and Approval Form for every project.
It could have four sections:
1. AI System Profile — purpose, business owner, model/provider, data used, users, and whether it can make automated decisions.
2. Risk Assessment — score factors such as impact, data sensitivity, autonomy, scale, security exposure, and third-party dependencies as Low/Medium/High.
3. Required Controls — map the resulting risk level to mandatory controls such as access management, encryption, human oversight, security testing, monitoring, and incident response.
4. Approval & Review — record the risk level, accountable owner, approval decision, exceptions, and review date.
We could also maintain an AI inventory linking each system to its assessment. That way, teams follow the same lightweight process for every project, while higher-risk systems automatically trigger additional review and controls.
